---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={"About — Auspicious Music"}
  description={"What Auspicious Music publishes, who writes it, and how to reach the publication."}
  canonicalPath={"/about/"}
  lang={"en"}
  noindex={false}
  loadStringField={false}
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<style is:global>
@layer components {
  .pg-head { padding-block: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem) clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); }
  .pg-head h1 { max-width: 17ch; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .pg-head .lede { margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 58ch; }
  .pg-head--dark { background: var(--dark); color: var(--dark-text); padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
  .pg-head--dark .crumbs { color: var(--dark-muted); }
  .pg-head--dark .crumbs a:hover { color: var(--dark-text); }
  .pg-head--dark .lede { color: var(--dark-muted); }

  .prose { max-width: var(--measure); }
  .prose > * + * { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.2rem + 1.2vw, 2rem); letter-spacing: -0.016em; margin-top: clamp(2.75rem, 5vw, 3.75rem); }
  .prose h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-top: 2rem; letter-spacing: -0.012em; }
  .prose p { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .prose a:not(.link):not(.btn) { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }

  .rule-list li {
    padding-block: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.75rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .rule-list li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .rule-list li::before {
    content: ""; inline-size: 7px; block-size: 7px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: transparent; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--line-strong); margin-top: 0.62rem;
  }
  .rule-list strong { color: var(--ink); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }

  .callout { border-left: 2px solid var(--ink); padding: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1.5rem; }
  .callout strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.375rem; }
  .callout p { color: var(--ink); }

  .facts { display: grid; gap: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--dark-line); margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .facts > div {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(8rem, 12rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem; padding-block: 0.875rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--dark-line-soft);
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .facts dt { color: var(--dark-muted); }
  .facts dd { color: var(--dark-text); }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .facts > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.1875rem; } }

  .timeline { position: relative; padding-left: 2rem; }
  .timeline::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 3px; top: 1.2rem; bottom: 1.2rem; width: 1px; background: var(--line-strong); }
  .timeline li { position: relative; padding-block: 1.125rem; }
  .timeline li + li { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .timeline li::before {
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: -2rem; top: 1.7rem;
    inline-size: 7px; block-size: 7px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--canvas); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--line-strong);
  }
  .timeline li:last-child::before { background: var(--ember-bright); box-shadow: none; }
  .timeline time { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta); letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--muted); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.375rem; }
  .timeline h3 { font-size: 1.125rem; letter-spacing: -0.011em; margin: 0 0 0.375rem; }
  .timeline p { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 58ch; }

  .listing li { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .listing li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .listing a {
    display: grid; gap: 0.375rem 2.5rem; padding-block: 1.375rem;
    text-decoration: none; align-items: baseline;
    transition: background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .listing a:hover { background: var(--surface); }
  .listing h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; letter-spacing: -0.014em; }
  .listing p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 58ch; }
  .listing__tail { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta); letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--muted); }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .listing a { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 16rem) minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 9rem); align-items: start; }
    .listing__tail { text-align: right; padding-top: 0.3rem; }
  }

  .glossary > div { padding-block: 1.125rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .glossary > div:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .glossary dt { font-weight: 550; font-size: 1.0625rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .glossary dd { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 0.25rem; max-width: 60ch; }

  .sources { margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .sources h2 { font-size: var(--t-h3); margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
  .sources ol { display: grid; gap: 0.875rem; counter-reset: src; }
  .sources li { counter-increment: src; padding-left: 2rem; position: relative; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted); }
  .sources li::before { content: counter(src); position: absolute; left: 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta); }
  .sources a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
}
</style>
</Fragment>

<main id="content">

  <section class="pg-head" data-od-id="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol>
          <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
          <li>About</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      
      <h1>About Auspicious Music</h1>
      <p class="lede">An independent publication for music production, sound design, recording and creative audio technology — relaunched under new ownership in 2026.</p>
      
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="band" data-od-id="about-body">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0">What this publication does</h2>
        <p>
          Auspicious Music writes about making music with computers and with instruments,
          and refuses to treat those as separate subjects. Ableton Live and Max for Live,
          sampling and synthesis, recording acoustic instruments and strings, arrangement,
          and writing music for film, video and occasions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every technical page states the software version it was tested against and the
          date of that test. Where something was researched rather than tested, the page
          says so in those words. That standard is set out in full in the
          <a href="/about/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Who it is for</h2>
        <ul class="rule-list">
          <li><div><strong>Producers and electronic musicians</strong>People working in a DAW who want a method rather than a preset.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Ableton and Max for Live users</strong>From a first session through to building devices that solve a specific problem.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Composers for film, video and media</strong>Writing to a brief, to a picture, and to a delivery specification.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Instrumentalists moving into production</strong>Players integrating an acoustic instrument into a digital workflow.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Small studios and creators</strong>Anyone with a practical recording or workflow problem and no technical department to ask.</div></li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="authors">Authors</h2>
        <p>
          Articles are currently credited to the editorial desk while the author records
          are being set up. This publication does not invent bylines: no article will
          carry a name that does not belong to a real person who wrote or reviewed it,
          and author pages will link to verifiable work.
        </p>

        <h2>Relationship to other projects</h2>
        <p>
          The publisher works on other things, including music and video projects. Where
          one of those is genuinely relevant to an article — a recording used as an
          example, a real project used as a case study — it may be linked, and the
          relationship is disclosed on the page. There are no such links in the
          navigation or the global footer, and no article exists in order to carry one.
        </p>

        <h2 id="contact">Contact and corrections</h2>
        <p>
          Corrections are welcome and are acted on. If a technical claim, a date, an
          attribution or a historical detail is wrong, it gets fixed and the change is
          recorded on the page. That applies with particular force to anything concerning
          the former operator of this domain.
        </p>
        <div class="callout">
          <p>
            <strong>Contact details are not yet published.</strong>
            They go live with the operator information required for the legal notice,
            rather than being put up as a placeholder address that nobody reads.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2>The domain's history</h2>
        <p>
          This address hosted a different music-technology site under a different operator
          between roughly 2013 and 2017, and was later exploited for spam while it lay
          dormant. That history is documented rather than hidden — see
          <a href="/about/history-and-relaunch/">history and relaunch</a> for the full account,
          and the <a href="/download/">archive</a> for the status of every historic
          resource.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section data-od-id="relaunch-notice">
    <div class="shell relaunch">
      <p>Auspicious Music was relaunched under new ownership in 2026. Historical
         references are preserved for context.</p>
      <a class="link" href="/about/history-and-relaunch/">Read the history and relaunch note
        <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
</BaseLayout>